          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "James and Harry had the same amount of money.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "James spent all his money on books that cost $6 and Harry spent all his on books costing $8.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "If they both had more than $50 but less than $90, how many books did they each buy?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "James: 12 books; Harry: 9 books.",
      "worked": "The LCM of 6 and 8 is $24$, but we need a common multiple greater than $50$ and less than $90$.\n\nMultiples of 6 between 50 and 90: $54,60,66,72,78,84$.\n\nMultiples of 8 between 50 and 90: $56,64,72,80,88$.\n\nThe only shared multiple is $72$, so each had $\\$72$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{James's books}&=72\\div6\\\\&=12\\\\\\text{Harry's books}&=72\\div8\\\\&=9\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 36
  },
